        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U5 | SKYLAB SKW92A (`SKW92A:SKW92A`) | Main compute / WiFi radio / 5-port Ethernet switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting the Ethernet transmit pair to ground will prevent LAN port 3 from functioning and may damage the SKW92A PHY if driven.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R2"],
      "pins": ["R2.1", "R2.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(Q2-G)", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "R2 value is '10' (10 ohms) in the netlist and SPICE deck.",
      "expected": "Specification states R2 is 10 kΩ (10,000 ohms) pull-up for Q2 gate.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R2\") (value \"10\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R2 (10 kΩ, pulling Q2's gate high/off by default)"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 10 Ω pull-up will draw excessive current when the SKW92A GPIO drives the gate low, potentially damaging the GPIO or MOSFET, and will not provide the intended weak pull-up.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 value is '0.1uF/16V' in the netlist.",
      "expected": "Specification states C1 should be 1 µF/25 V (part of the C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 group).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"}
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost/charge-pump circuit will have incorrect capacitance and a lower voltage margin, potentially causing unstable display power or capacitor failure.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: U5 Ethernet pins 13/14 are shorted to ground, R2 is 10 Ω instead of 10 kΩ, and C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of 1 µF/25 V."
}

